Raw widefield fluorescence images supporting:
Weible AP, Wehr M (2022) Amyloid Pathology in the Central Auditory Pathway of 5XFAD Mice Appears First in
Auditory Cortex. J Alzheimers Dis 89(4):1385-1402. doi:10.3233/JAD-220538. PMCID: PMC10097438.

Hemizygous 5XFAD mice (JAX 006554, B6SJL hybrid background) were perfused at P14-P150; brains were cut in
30 um coronal sections and labeled with anti-Abeta42 (Invitrogen 700254; Alexa Fluor 488 secondary) and DAPI.
Images were acquired on a Zeiss Axio Imager A2 with an AxioCam MRm3 camera in ZEN 3.1, one channel per image.
Wild-type controls showed no detectable label and were not imaged.

FILE FORMAT. Images are single-channel OME-TIFF. Where the original .czi survives intact they hold the
12-bit raw data (uint16). For a minority of images the .czi was missing or corrupted (including all images
of mice 0245, 0242 and 0393); these were converted from ZEN's 8-bit .jpg export (display-scaled, signal
channel only) and are marked SourceFormat / source_format = jpg.
Note that CZI-derived images are 12-bit data in uint16; adjust display range to 0–4095 if the images appear dark.

MAGNIFICATION. The microscope's objectives are changed by hand, and the objective recorded by ZEN is not
reliable. Magnification was therefore inferred from image content, and pixel size derived from it:
  acq-12p5x  overview, 1.25x objective (12.5X total with 10x eyepiece), 5.16 um/pixel
  acq-100x   10x objective (100X total), 0.645 um/pixel
  acq-200x   20x objective (200X total), 0.3225 um/pixel
DAPI images were classified from nucleus size; Abeta42 and red images take the class of the DAPI image of the
same field (matched by image similarity), and Abeta42 focal stacks without a matching DAPI image are 200X,
following the imaging protocol. Each image's sidecar gives MagnificationSource and MagnificationConfidence; please confirm the scale visually before making quantitative measurements.

ORGANIZATION. Each image sequence begins with low-magnification coronal overviews used to locate the
high-magnification fields of view in each region examined. High-magnification fields include several Abeta42
images (stain-Abeta42) at different focal depths, DAPI images (stain-DAPI), and, where needed, a red-channel
image (stain-autofluorescence) to distinguish antibody label from autofluorescence. If no images of a region
are included for a mouse, no label was judged present at the time of imaging.

Images for each mouse were acquired in a main imaging pass followed, for many mice, by later targeted
rounds (e.g. follow-up imaging, or region-specific rounds for subiculum, MGB, SOC, PRNc) that may or may not
be of the same sections. These rounds are not split into BIDS sessions because all images come from the same
fixed tissue; the acquisition time and original subfolder of every image are listed in sub-<ID>_scans.tsv.
run-<N> is the original ZEN snapshot number (Snap-N); where ZEN reused a snapshot number within a mouse,
later repeats are numbered N+100000. The imaged region, where recorded in the original folder name, is given
in each image's BodyPartDetails and in scans.tsv; n/a means not recorded.
